{"id":"CVE-2014-10064","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2018-05-31T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-17T00:36:04.821Z","description":"The qs module before 1.0.0 does not have an option or default for specifying object depth and when parsing a string representing a deeply nested object will block the event loop for long periods of time. An attacker could leverage this to cause a temporary denial-of-service condition, for example, in a web application, other requests would not be processed while this blocking is occurring.","cwe":["CWE-400 Denial of Service (CWE-400)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"HackerOne","product":"qs node module","versions":["affected <1.0.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://nodesecurity.io/advisories/28","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
